+body from `s.replace(",", " ")` to `s.replace(",", "x")`; the original
+postcondition is retained. Satisfying witness: input `","` (CS = [44]) makes
+the original return `[]` and the mutant return `["x"]`.
+
+COMMAND:
+kompile verification-body-mutant.k --backend haskell --main-module WORDS-STRING-BODY-MUTANT --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --output-definition body-mutant-kompiled
+
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+WALL TIME: 4.59 s
+RELEVANT OUTPUT:
+Only the supplied strLt unused-variable warnings.
+
+COMMAND:
+kprove spec-body-mutant.k --definition body-mutant-kompiled --spec-module WORDS-STRING-BODY-MUTANT-SPEC
+
+EXIT STATUS: 1
+WALL TIME: 3.47 s
+RELEVANT OUTPUT:
+kore-exec: Warning (WarnStuckClaimState):
+  #Ceil(splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 120), .IntSeq, .ValSeq))
+  #And
+  #Not(
+    #Ceil(splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 32), .IntSeq, .ValSeq))
+    #And {
+      splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 32), .IntSeq, .ValSeq)
+      #Equals
+      splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 120), .IntSeq, .ValSeq)
+    })
+...
+<heap>
+  0 |-> list(splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 120), .IntSeq, .ValSeq))
+</heap>
+[Error] Prover: backend terminated because the configuration cannot be
+rewritten further.
+
+This confirms body sensitivity and shows that the theorem executes the body
+term, rather than consulting an answer oracle detached from it.
