+Fresh false-postcondition mutation
+==================================
+
+Mutation:
+The original successful postcondition requires heap object 0 to contain
+`list(wordsStringExpected(CS))`. The mutation prepends the extra word `"x"`:
+`list(vCons(str(iCons(120, .IntSeq)), wordsStringExpected(CS)))`.
+The precondition and executed program are unchanged. For satisfying witness
+CS = .IntSeq (Python input ""), the program returns `[]`, while the mutated
+postcondition requires `["x"]`.
+
+COMMAND:
+kprove spec-vacuity-audit.k --definition verification-kompiled --spec-module WORDS-STRING-SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT --dry-run
+
+EXIT STATUS: 0
+WALL TIME: 1.99 s
+RELEVANT OUTPUT:
+kore-exec .../verification-kompiled/definition.kore
+  --module WORDS-STRING-VERIFICATION
+  --prove .../spec.kore
+  --spec-module WORDS-STRING-SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT ...
+
+This establishes that the mutation parsed and built successfully.
+
+COMMAND:
+kprove spec-vacuity-audit.k --definition verification-kompiled --spec-module WORDS-STRING-SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT
+
+EXIT STATUS: 1
+WALL TIME: 3.29 s
+RELEVANT OUTPUT:
+kore-exec: Warning (WarnStuckClaimState):
+  #Ceil(splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 32), .IntSeq, .ValSeq))
+  #And
+  #Not({
+    splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 32), .IntSeq, .ValSeq)
+    #Equals
+    vCons(str(iCons(120, .IntSeq)),
+      splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 32), .IntSeq, .ValSeq))
+  })
+...
+<heap>
+  0 |-> list(splitWS(replaceC(CS, 44, 32), .IntSeq, .ValSeq))
+</heap>
+[Error] Prover: backend terminated because the configuration cannot be
+rewritten further.
+
+The failure is the intended unmet result equality after normal execution, not a
+parser error, timeout, unrelated crash, or unreachable mutation.
